  m_text: "<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 106</b></color></size>\n<b>A manuscript of the Rigveda</b>\n<size=74%>Hymns composed c. 1500\u20131200 BCE; manuscript 19th century\n<i>Ink on paper, Devanagari script</i>\nLater manuscript copy</size>\n<size=70%><line-height=110%>\nThe Rigveda is a collection of 1,028 hymns in Vedic Sanskrit, composed in north-western India and passed down by word of mouth with remarkable precision for many centuries before being written down. Manuscripts like this are much later copies.</size>\n<size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Photo: Ms Sarah Welch / CC BY-SA 4.0 / Wikimedia Commons</color></size>"
