  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 107</b></color></size>\n<b>Punch-marked coins</b>\n<size=74%>c. 6th\u20132nd century BCE\n<i>Silver</i>\nVarious museum collections</size>\n<size=70%><line-height=110%>\nIndia's earliest coins were small pieces of silver stamped with symbols such as the sun, animals, trees and hills, one punch at a time. They circulated in the Mahajanapadas \u2013 'great realms' such as Magadha, Kosala and Avanti \u2013 as trade and cities grew in the Ganga plain.</size>\n<size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Photo: Unknown / Public domain / Wikimedia Commons</color></size>"
